Why Is Demand Increasing?
Growth of event-driven applications: Microservices and distributed applications rely on dependable messaging systems to exchange events and coordinate business processes.
Demand for real-time data: Financial services, industrial IoT, and digital platforms require high-throughput infrastructure to process events with minimal delay.
Cloud-native modernization: Organizations are adopting scalable messaging and streaming platforms to support containerized applications, hybrid environments, and distributed workloads.

High-Performance Messaging Watch: Edge Computing and Event Streaming
Messaging infrastructure is evolving toward cloud-native streaming, distributed brokers, and low-latency event delivery. Edge deployments are becoming relevant for applications that need rapid local processing, including industrial monitoring and connected mobility. Providers are also working to improve interoperability, observability, and security across hybrid and multicloud environments without compromising performance.

